# Spec for tools/riscpkg.py: the HEIF and AVIF plug-in for Lumen.
Package: LumenHEIF
Section: Graphics
Priority: Optional
Licence: Free
Maintainer: Andrew Youll <adyoull@users.noreply.github.com>
Standards-Version: 0.4.0
Environment: arm32, vfpv3
Depends: Lumen (>= 0.0.37)
Homepage: https://github.com/adyoull/riscos-lumen
Description: HEIF and AVIF photos in Lumen
 The LumenHEIF plug-in lets Lumen open HEIF photos (.heic, .heif, .hif),
 as iPhones and many other phones and cameras save them, and AVIF photos
 (.avif). It reads 8, 10 and 12-bit and tiled photos, and turns Display
 P3 into sRGB. Built on libheif 1.23.7, FFmpeg's HEVC decoder and dav1d.
 Decoding a 12 MP photo needs about 100 MB of free memory. It goes into
 Lumen's Plugins directory, with its own guide.
Build-Map: !Lumen/Plugins/HEIF -> Apps/Graphics/!Lumen/Plugins/HEIF
Build-Notice: LumenHEIF, packaged for PackMan from the release zip on
 https://github.com/adyoull/riscos-lumen/releases
 .
 LumenHEIF's own code is under the MIT licence. It is linked with
 libheif (GNU LGPL 3), FFmpeg's HEVC decoder (GNU LGPL 2.1 or later) and
 dav1d (BSD 2-clause); their sources and the RISC OS changes are on the
 release page (LumenHEIF-1.3-sources.zip). The notices follow.
Build-Copyright: !Lumen/Plugins/HEIF/Licence
